# Paths with no owner below merge on one approving review, and CodeRabbit's
# automatic approval counts as that review (.coderabbit.yaml). A GitHub App
# cannot be a code owner, so the old catch-all line that named the approver
# bot is gone: "Without an owner, changes ... can be made with the approval of
# any user who has write access to the repository."
# https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
# https://docs.coderabbit.ai/pr-reviews/approval-policies
# The owner-only block keeps the gate, the checks and the reserved classes his:
# GitHub's Actions hardening guide says to code-own workflow files. Last match wins.

# Agent rules stay the owner's, even where they sit among unowned docs.
**/AGENTS.md                @nish3451
/CLAUDE.md                  @nish3451

# The owner alone: the review gate, the
# checks, the schema, money, sign-in, data deletion and privacy promises.
/.github/                   @nish3451
# CodeRabbit reads this file from the branch under review, so a pull request
# could loosen its own review; the owner signs off on every change to it.
# https://docs.coderabbit.ai/getting-started/yaml-configuration
/.coderabbit.yaml           @nish3451
